1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,020
Welcome to My Funnels in Authors Bureau.

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:07,161
This is where a published offer becomes a guided reader journey.

3
00:00:07,161 --> 00:00:09,570
Begin by selecting the correct book.

4
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:13,007
The book selector controls which products and funnels you see.

5
00:00:13,007 --> 00:00:17,916
Choosing the title first prevents one book's funnel from being confused with another.

6
00:00:17,916 --> 00:00:23,046
If ABBY can build a funnel for a published product, open the suggestions panel.

7
00:00:23,046 --> 00:00:29,179
Suggestions are grouped by purpose: opt-in, sales, application, or event.

8
00:00:29,179 --> 00:00:30,937
Choose the product once.

9
00:00:30,937 --> 00:00:35,755
ABBY creates one associated funnel and places it in the selected book view.

10
00:00:35,755 --> 00:00:39,427
Each funnel card shows the stages a reader will move through.

11
00:00:39,427 --> 00:00:42,005
Open a stage to review its details.

12
00:00:42,005 --> 00:00:47,643
An opt-in funnel may include a landing page, form, delivery, and follow-up.

13
00:00:47,643 --> 00:00:53,190
A sales funnel may include the offer, checkout, confirmation, and fulfilment.

14
00:00:53,190 --> 00:00:55,703
The exact stages depend on the offer.

15
00:00:55,703 --> 00:01:01,484
Use Edit copy when the headline, supporting text, or call to action needs adjustment.

16
00:01:01,484 --> 00:01:03,984
Save your changes to the existing funnel.

17
00:01:03,984 --> 00:01:07,968
You do not need to regenerate approved copy just to make a small edit.

18
00:01:07,968 --> 00:01:13,489
Before publication, Authors Bureau checks that every required stage is ready.

19
00:01:13,489 --> 00:01:20,677
If Publish funnel is unavailable, open the stages that need attention and complete the missing details.

20
00:01:20,677 --> 00:01:27,486
This protects readers from reaching an unfinished form, missing delivery, or incomplete destination.

21
00:01:27,486 --> 00:01:31,093
When every stage is ready, publish the funnel.

22
00:01:31,093 --> 00:01:36,406
Then use Open to inspect the live result and Copy link to share the public address.

23
00:01:36,406 --> 00:01:41,432
Publishing changes the existing funnel to live; it does not create a duplicate.

24
00:01:41,432 --> 00:01:45,455
The More menu includes Change book for association corrections.

25
00:01:45,455 --> 00:01:49,127
Use it only when a funnel belongs to another existing book.

26
00:01:49,127 --> 00:01:51,744
This changes the association only.

27
00:01:51,744 --> 00:01:58,346
It does not rewrite the funnel, alter its leads, or assign unattributed funnels automatically.

28
00:01:58,346 --> 00:02:01,419
You can pause a live funnel without deleting it.

29
00:02:01,419 --> 00:02:05,468
The saved stages and copy remain available for later review.

30
00:02:05,468 --> 00:02:15,507
The reliable workflow is: select the book, create from the correct product, review every stage, publish once, and verify the live link.

31
00:02:15,507 --> 00:02:16,861
Authors Bureau.

32
00:02:16,861 --> 00:02:18,854
Your Story is Your LIFE.

